libfdt, fdtput: fix discarded const qualifiers with newer glibc

Newer glibc (2.43+) declares type-generic overloads for memchr()/
strrchr() and similar functions so that calling them with a `const
char *` argument returns a `const`-qualified pointer, instead of
always returning a plain (non-const) pointer as older glibc did. This
is stricter and more correct, but it turns two pre-existing constness
mismatches in dtc into hard errors under GCC (assignment discards
'const' qualifier from pointer target type
[-Werror=discarded-qualifiers]), since dtc builds with -Werror:

  libfdt/fdt_overlay.c: In function 'overlay_fixup_phandle':
  libfdt/fdt_overlay.c:424:21: error: assignment discards 'const'
  qualifier from pointer target type [-Werror=discarded-qualifiers]
          sep = memchr(fixup_str, ':', fixup_len);

  fdtput.c: In function 'create_node':
  fdtput.c:235:11: error: assignment discards 'const' qualifier from
  pointer target type [-Werror=discarded-qualifiers]
          p = strrchr(node_name, '/');

In overlay_fixup_phandle(), `sep` is only ever read through, never
written to, so it can simply become `const char *`.

In create_node(), `p` is used to write into the string
(`*p = '\0'`) even though the function's own `node_name` parameter is
declared `const char *` — this already relied on the caller passing a
mutable buffer under a const-qualified type, which the new glibc
overloads no longer let slip through silently. Take an owned mutable
copy with the existing xstrdup() helper and operate on that instead,
freeing it on every return path.

Backported from the fix already applied upstream in dtc v1.8.0
(github.com/dgibson/dtc, issue #180), adapted to this dtc 1.7.2 tree
(upstream's newer xstrndup()-based version isn't needed here; the
existing xstrdup() helper in util.c/util.h covers this case).

Signed-off-by: Ilko Iliev <ilko.iliev@gmail.com>

--- a/libfdt/fdt_overlay.c	2026-09-14 11:10:06.865737440 +0000
+++ b/libfdt/fdt_overlay.c	2026-09-14 11:10:06.929895187 +0000
@@ -409,7 +409,8 @@
 		const char *fixup_str = value;
 		uint32_t path_len, name_len;
 		uint32_t fixup_len;
-		char *sep, *endptr;
+		const char *sep;
+		char *endptr;
 		int poffset, ret;
 
 		fixup_end = memchr(value, '\0', len);
--- a/fdtput.c	2026-09-14 11:10:06.868223062 +0000
+++ b/fdtput.c	2026-09-14 11:10:06.930194635 +0000
@@ -230,21 +230,24 @@
 static int create_node(char **blob, const char *node_name)
 {
 	int node = 0;
+	char *name = xstrdup(node_name);
 	char *p;
 
-	p = strrchr(node_name, '/');
+	p = strrchr(name, '/');
 	if (!p) {
 		report_error(node_name, -1, -FDT_ERR_BADPATH);
+		free(name);
 		return -1;
 	}
 	*p = '\0';
 
 	*blob = realloc_node(*blob, p + 1);
 
-	if (p > node_name) {
-		node = fdt_path_offset(*blob, node_name);
+	if (p > name) {
+		node = fdt_path_offset(*blob, name);
 		if (node < 0) {
-			report_error(node_name, -1, node);
+			report_error(name, -1, node);
+			free(name);
 			return -1;
 		}
 	}
@@ -252,9 +255,11 @@
 	node = fdt_add_subnode(*blob, node, p + 1);
 	if (node < 0) {
 		report_error(p + 1, -1, node);
+		free(name);
 		return -1;
 	}
 
+	free(name);
 	return 0;
 }
 
